source	Plato, Republic I 353d-354a, tr. B. Jowett
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 1497, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/1497
class	equivocation
at	S16	And he who lives well is blessed and happy
fault	"live well" moves from functioning well (as the soul's excellence) to faring well (being happy)
reference	J. Annas, An Introduction to Plato's Republic (1981), ch. 2
